  - chiral interactions
  - self-assembly
  - particle simulation

abstract: >-
  ChiSurfMD is a modular C++20 molecular-dynamics framework for
  two-dimensional particle systems with configurable anisotropic and chiral
  interactions. It provides interchangeable particle models, interaction
  potentials, numerical integrators, and thermostats, together with ADIOS2
  output, scripted simulation workflows, and Python/Jupyter analysis tools.
  The software was developed for specialized self-assembly studies and rapid
  testing of custom two-dimensional interaction models.
